---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GrievanceOfficer from '../components/GrievanceOfficer.astro';

// Dynamic (not prerendered) because BaseLayout's nav/footer depend on
// live per-request session and locale state via Astro.cookies.
export const prerender = false;

// Written from the business's actual booking, payment, and cancellation
// practices; not yet reviewed by a lawyer. Have it reviewed, particularly
// the liability and governing-law sections. This used to be a public
// banner, removed 26 Sep 2026 because payment-network reviewers read it as
// an incomplete policy.
// Apple sign-in is built but not switched on, so only Google and email are
// named under Accounts (same in privacy.astro); add Apple back when it is.
// The business details in the intro match /about and /contact.
const lastUpdated = '27 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service — IWIS Global" description="The terms and conditions that apply when you book a Taj Mahal or Agra tour with IWIS Global.">
  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-serif font-semibold mb-1">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mb-6">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      These terms apply when you book a tour through this website, operated by IWIS Global ("we", "us"), a
      partnership firm based in Agra, Uttar Pradesh, India (GSTIN 09AAIFI6799J1ZH), whose registered address is
      A-5, First Floor, ESSAR Mughal Residency, Jyoti Nagar, Shaheed Nagar, Agra – 282001. By booking a tour,
      you agree to them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Booking and payment</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-stone-700 space-y-1 mb-6">
      <li>The price shown on the tour page at checkout — including any add-ons you select — is the price you pay. There are no hidden fees.</li>
      <li>Payments are processed securely by Razorpay. Prices are quoted in Indian Rupees (INR), with US Dollar (USD) pricing available for tours where we've set a USD rate.</li>
      <li>You can pay the full price, or a 25% deposit online to secure your booking with the balance paid on pickup. If you cancel, any refund is worked out on the amount you paid.</li>
      <li>Your booking is confirmed once payment succeeds; you'll receive confirmation immediately.</li>
      <li>You don't need to create an account to book — an account is only needed if you want to see your booking history for tours you book while signed in.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">How late you can book</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      Tours can be booked until 9 PM India Standard Time (IST) the night before, to allow time to arrange your
      vehicle and guide. After 9 PM, the earliest date you can book is the day after tomorrow. Tours don't run
      on Fridays, when the Taj Mahal is closed.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Cancellations, refunds, and date changes</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      You can cancel for a full refund up to 24 hours before your tour's scheduled start time; cancellations
      made less than 24 hours before receive a 50% refund, and no-shows aren't refunded. Date changes are free
      up to 24 hours before, subject to availability. To cancel, contact us using the details below. Full
      details, including refund timelines and what happens if we cancel, are in our
      <a href="/cancellation-refund-policy" class="text-brand-800 hover:underline">Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Your responsibilities</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-stone-700 space-y-1 mb-6">
      <li>Provide accurate traveler details (name, contact information, number of travelers) at the time of booking.</li>
      <li>Arrive at the agreed pickup point and time — tours may not be able to wait for late arrivals.</li>
      <li>Carry valid ID and any tickets/permits required for the sites visited (e.g. the Taj Mahal), where applicable.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Changes and disruptions</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      Tours may occasionally be affected by circumstances outside our control — site closures, weather,
      traffic, or local restrictions. If we have to cancel your tour, you choose a full refund of everything
      you've paid or a free change to a new date, as set out in our
      <a href="/cancellation-refund-policy" class="text-brand-800 hover:underline">Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy</a>.
      Otherwise, we'll work with you to resolve the issue; we are not responsible for losses caused by such
      circumstances beyond our control.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Accounts</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      Signing in with Google, or with an email and password, is optional and only used to show you your own
      booking history. You're responsible for keeping your sign-in details secure.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      We may update these terms from time to time; the "last updated" date above reflects the most recent
      change. Continuing to use the site after an update means you accept the revised terms.
    </p>

    <GrievanceOfficer />

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Governing law</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      These terms are governed by the laws of India, where this business operates.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Contact us</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700">
      Questions about these terms, or to cancel a booking, contact us at
      <a href="mailto:info@iwisglobal.com" class="text-brand-800 hover:underline">info@iwisglobal.com</a> or via
      <a href={`https://wa.me/916399226633?text=${encodeURIComponent('Hi! (ref: TERMS)')}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-wa-ref="TERMS" class="text-brand-800 hover:underline">WhatsApp</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
